    "q-333055": {
      "dom_id": "step-q333055",
      "name": "Question 7",
      "problem": "$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}^{′}(t)=3{x}_{1}(t)-2 \\\\ {x}_{2}^{′}(t)=2{x}_{1}(t)+5{x}_{2}(t),\\end{aligned}\\,x(0)=[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nConsider the initial value problem above. By applying the Laplace transform $L$ to both sides of each equation in our system, we get a system with variables ${X}_{1}(s)=L\\{{x}_{1}(t)\\}$ and ${X}_{2}(s)=L\\{{x}_{2}(t)\\}.$ In terms of the parameter $s,$ the solution of the new system is\n\n${X}_{1}(s)=-\\frac{s+2}{s(s-3)},\\,$\n${X}_{2}(s)=$ {{field-1}}.",
      "worked_solution": "First, we compute the Laplace transforms of both sides of each equation in our system:\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}L\\{{x}_{1}^{′}(t)\\}=L\\{3{x}_{1}(t)-2\\} \\\\ L\\{{x}_{2}^{′}(t)\\}=L\\{2{x}_{1}(t)+5{x}_{2}(t)\\}\\end{aligned}\\,\\,\n$$\n\nUsing the derivative property of the Laplace transform, we obtain the system\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}sL\\{{x}_{1}(t)\\}-{x}_{1}(0)=3L\\{{x}_{1}(t)\\}-2L\\{1\\} \\\\ sL\\{{x}_{2}(t)\\}-{x}_{2}(0)=2L\\{{x}_{1}(t)\\}+5L\\{{x}_{2}(t)\\}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich can be simplified to the following:\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}s{X}_{1}(s)+1=3{X}_{1}(s)-\\frac{2}{s} \\\\ s{X}_{2}(s)-4=2{X}_{1}(s)+5{X}_{2}(s)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere ${X}_{1}(s)=L\\{{x}_{1}(t)\\}$ and ${X}_{2}(s)=L\\{{x}_{2}(t)\\},$ and we have used the fact that $L\\{1\\}=\\frac{1}{s}.$\n\nNow, solving the first equation for ${X}_{1}(s),$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}s{X}_{1}(s)+1 & =3{X}_{1}(s)-\\frac{2}{s} \\\\ (s-3){X}_{1}(s) & =-1-\\frac{2}{s} \\\\ (s-3){X}_{1}(s) & =-(1+\\frac{2}{s}) \\\\ (s-3){X}_{1}(s) & =-(\\frac{s+2}{s}) \\\\ {X}_{1}(s) & =-\\frac{s+2}{s(s-3)}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting this in the second equation and solving for ${X}_{2}(s),$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}s{X}_{2}(s)-4 & =2{X}_{1}(s)+5{X}_{2}(s) \\\\ (s-5){X}_{2}(s) & =2{X}_{1}(s)+4 \\\\ (s-5){X}_{2}(s) & =2(-\\frac{s+2}{s(s-3)})+4 \\\\ (s-5){X}_{2}(s) & =-\\frac{2(s+2)}{s(s-3)}+4 \\\\ (s-5){X}_{2}(s) & =\\frac{-2(s+2)+4s(s-3)}{s(s-3)} \\\\ (s-5){X}_{2}(s) & =\\frac{-2s-4+4{s}^{2}-12s}{s(s-3)} \\\\ (s-5){X}_{2}(s) & =\\frac{4{s}^{2}-14s-4}{s(s-3)} \\\\ {X}_{2}(s) & =\\frac{4{s}^{2}-14s-4}{s(s-3)(s-5)}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution of the new system in terms of parameter $s$ is \n\n$$\n{X}_{1}(s)=-\\frac{s+2}{s(s-3)},\\,{X}_{2}(s)=\\frac{4{s}^{2}-14s-4}{s(s-3)(s-5)}.\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
