    "q-332785": {
      "dom_id": "step-q332785",
      "name": "Question 9",
      "problem": "$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}^{′}(t)=3{x}_{1}(t) \\\\ {x}_{2}^{′}(t)=-2{x}_{1}(t)+{x}_{2}(t)+3,\\end{aligned}\\,x(0)=[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nConsider the initial value problem above. By applying the Laplace transform $L$ to both sides of each equation in our system, we get a system with variables ${X}_{1}(s)=L\\{{x}_{1}(t)\\}$ and ${X}_{2}(s)=L\\{{x}_{2}(t)\\}.$ In terms of the parameter $s,$ the solution of the new system is\n\n${X}_{1}(s)=-\\frac{1}{s-3},\\,$\n${X}_{2}(s)=$ {{field-1}}.",
      "worked_solution": "First, we compute the Laplace transforms of both sides of each equation in our system:\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}L\\{{x}_{1}^{′}(t)\\}=L\\{3{x}_{1}(t)\\} \\\\ L\\{{x}_{2}^{′}(t)\\}=L\\{-2{x}_{1}(t)+{x}_{2}(t)+3\\}\\end{aligned}\\,\\,\n$$\n\nUsing the derivative property of the Laplace transform, we obtain the system\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}sL\\{{x}_{1}(t)\\}-{x}_{1}(0)=3L\\{{x}_{1}(t)\\} \\\\ sL\\{{x}_{2}(t)\\}-{x}_{2}(0)=-2L\\{{x}_{1}(t)\\}+L\\{{x}_{2}(t)\\}+3L\\{1\\}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich can be simplified to the following:\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}s{X}_{1}(s)+1=3{X}_{1}(s) \\\\ s{X}_{2}(s)-2=-2{X}_{1}(s)+{X}_{2}(s)+\\frac{3}{s}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere ${X}_{1}(s)=L\\{{x}_{1}(t)\\}$ and ${X}_{2}(s)=L\\{{x}_{2}(t)\\},$ and we have used the fact that $L\\{1\\}=\\frac{1}{s}.$\n\nNow, solving the first equation for ${X}_{1}(s),$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}s{X}_{1}(s)+1 & =3{X}_{1}(s) \\\\ (s-3){X}_{1}(s) & =-1 \\\\ {X}_{1}(s) & =-\\frac{1}{s-3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting this in the second equation and solving for ${X}_{2}(s),$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}s{X}_{2}(s)-2 & =-2{X}_{1}(s)+{X}_{2}(s)+\\frac{3}{s} \\\\ (s-1){X}_{2}(s) & =-2{X}_{1}(s)+2+\\frac{3}{s} \\\\ (s-1){X}_{2}(s) & =-2(-\\frac{1}{s-3})+2+\\frac{3}{s} \\\\ (s-1){X}_{2}(s) & =(\\frac{2}{s-3})+(\\frac{2s+3}{s}) \\\\ (s-1){X}_{2}(s) & =\\frac{2s+(2s+3)(s-3)}{s(s-3)} \\\\ (s-1){X}_{2}(s) & =\\frac{2s+(2{s}^{2}-3s-9)}{s(s-3)} \\\\ (s-1){X}_{2}(s) & =\\frac{2{s}^{2}-s-9}{s(s-3)} \\\\ {X}_{2}(s) & =\\frac{2{s}^{2}-s-9}{s(s-1)(s-3)}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution of the new system in terms of parameter $s$ is \n\n$$\n{X}_{1}(s)=-\\frac{1}{s-3},\\,{X}_{2}(s)=\\frac{2{s}^{2}-s-9}{s(s-1)(s-3)}.\n$$",
