    "q-333061": {
      "dom_id": "step-q333061",
      "name": "Question 10",
      "problem": "$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}^{′}(t)=-2{x}_{1}(t) \\\\ {x}_{2}^{′}(t)=3{x}_{1}(t)+4{x}_{2}(t)+5,\\end{aligned}\\,x(0)=[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nConsider the initial value problem above. By applying the Laplace transform $L$ to both sides of each equation in our system, we get a system with variables ${X}_{1}(s)=L\\{{x}_{1}(t)\\}$ and ${X}_{2}(s)=L\\{{x}_{2}(t)\\}.$ In terms of the parameter $s,$ the solution of the new system is\n\n${X}_{1}(s)=-\\frac{3}{s+2},\\,$\n${X}_{2}(s)=$ {{field-1}}.",
      "worked_solution": "First, we compute the Laplace transforms of both sides of each equation in our system:\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}L\\{{x}_{1}^{′}(t)\\}=L\\{-2{x}_{1}(t)\\} \\\\ L\\{{x}_{2}^{′}(t)\\}=L\\{3{x}_{1}(t)+4{x}_{2}(t)+5\\}\\end{aligned}\\,\\,\n$$\n\nUsing the derivative property of the Laplace transform, we obtain the system\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}sL\\{{x}_{1}(t)\\}-{x}_{1}(0)=-2L\\{{x}_{1}(t)\\} \\\\ sL\\{{x}_{2}(t)\\}-{x}_{2}(0)=3L\\{{x}_{1}(t)\\}+4L\\{{x}_{2}(t)\\}+5L\\{1\\}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich can be simplified to the following:\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}s{X}_{1}(s)+3=-2{X}_{1}(s) \\\\ s{X}_{2}(s)-1=3{X}_{1}(s)+4{X}_{2}(s)+\\frac{5}{s}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere ${X}_{1}(s)=L\\{{x}_{1}(t)\\}$ and ${X}_{2}(s)=L\\{{x}_{2}(t)\\},$ and we have used the fact that $L\\{1\\}=\\frac{1}{s}.$\n\nNow, solving the first equation for ${X}_{1}(s),$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}s{X}_{1}(s)+3 & =-2{X}_{1}(s) \\\\ (s+2){X}_{1}(s) & =-3 \\\\ {X}_{1}(s) & =-\\frac{3}{s+2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting this in the second equation and solving for ${X}_{2}(s),$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}s{X}_{2}(s)-1 & =3{X}_{1}(s)+4{X}_{2}(s)+\\frac{5}{s} \\\\ (s-4){X}_{2}(s) & =3{X}_{1}(s)+\\frac{5}{s}+1 \\\\ (s-4){X}_{2}(s) & =3(-\\frac{3}{s+2})+\\frac{5+s}{s} \\\\ (s-4){X}_{2}(s) & =-\\frac{9}{s+2}+\\frac{5+s}{s} \\\\ (s-4){X}_{2}(s) & =-\\frac{9s}{s(s+2)}+\\frac{(5+s)(s+2)}{s(s+2)} \\\\ (s-4){X}_{2}(s) & =\\frac{-9s+(5+s)(s+2)}{s(s+2)} \\\\ (s-4){X}_{2}(s) & =\\frac{-9s+5s+{s}^{2}+10+2s}{s(s+2)} \\\\ {X}_{2}(s) & =\\frac{{s}^{2}-2s+10}{s(s+2)(s-4)}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution of the new system in terms of parameter $s$ is \n\n$$\n{X}_{1}(s)=-\\frac{3}{s+2},\\,{X}_{2}(s)=\\frac{{s}^{2}-2s+10}{s(s+2)(s-4)}.\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
      "fields": [
        {
          "key": "field-1",
