      "source_example_id": "e-21577",
      "knowledge_point": "Solving an Initial Value Problem Given the Laplace Transformed Solution",
      "kp_id": "e-21577"
    },
    "q-333124": {
      "dom_id": "step-q333124",
      "name": "Question 14",
      "problem": "$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}^{′}(t)={x}_{1}(t)+3 \\\\ {x}_{2}^{′}(t)=-2{x}_{1}(t)+3{x}_{2}(t)-3,\\end{aligned}\\,x(0)=[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nConsider the initial value problem above. By applying the Laplace transform to both sides of each equation in our system, we get a transformed system with the solution \n\n$$\n{X}_{1}(s)=L\\{{x}_{1}(t)\\}=\\frac{1}{s-1}-\\frac{3}{s},\\,{X}_{2}(s)=L\\{{x}_{2}(t)\\}=\\frac{1}{s-1}-\\frac{1}{s}+\\frac{2}{s-3}.\n$$\n\nFind the solution to the original initial value problem.\n\n<table align=\"l\" cellpadding=\"0\" rules=\"all\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td rowspan=\"2\" height=\"35px\" align=\"center\">$x(t)=\\,\\,$</td>\n<td width=\"5px\" height=\"40px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\">{{field-1}}</td>\n<td width=\"5px\" align=\"center\"></td>\n<td rowspan=\"2\" height=\"40px\" align=\"center\"></td>\n</tr>\n\n<tr>\n<td width=\"5px\" height=\"35px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\">{{field-2}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\"></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>",
      "worked_solution": "To find ${x}_{1}(t)$ and ${x}_{2}(t)$ satisfying the original initial value problem, we apply the inverse Laplace transform to ${X}_{1}(s)$ and ${X}_{2}(s):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}(t) & ={L}^{-1}\\{{X}_{1}(s)\\} \\\\  & ={L}^{-1}\\{\\frac{1}{s-1}-\\frac{3}{s}\\} \\\\  & ={L}^{-1}\\{\\frac{1}{s-1}\\}-3{L}^{-1}\\{\\frac{1}{s}\\} \\\\  & ={e}^{1\\cdot t}-3\\cdot 1 \\\\  & ={e}^{t}-3 \\\\ {x}_{2}(t) & ={L}^{-1}\\{{X}_{2}(s)\\} \\\\  & ={L}^{-1}\\{\\frac{1}{s-1}-\\frac{1}{s}+\\frac{2}{s-3}\\} \\\\  & ={L}^{-1}\\{\\frac{1}{s-1}\\}-{L}^{-1}\\{\\frac{1}{s}\\}+2\\,{L}^{-1}\\{\\frac{1}{s-3}\\} \\\\  & ={e}^{1\\cdot t}-1+2{e}^{3\\cdot t} \\\\  & ={e}^{t}+2{e}^{3t}-1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we write down the solution to the initial value problem:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(t) & =[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}(t) \\\\ {x}_{2}(t)\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}{e}^{t}-3 \\\\ {e}^{t}+2{e}^{3t}-1\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
